    "question": {
      ":question/id": "bd5247a9-26cc-53ee-9683-ec070f810aa5",
      ":question/problem": "Find $l$, if $6{a}_{1}+l{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}54 \\\\ -24 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $l$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{a}_{1}+l{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 6\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+l\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}54 \\\\ -24 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ l\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}54 \\\\ -24 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}-6\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ l\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -24\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $l=-3.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
